# Line-ending policy for the cross-platform launcher/uninstaller scripts.
# A .command/.sh with CRLF fails under bash (the trailing \r breaks the
# shebang and every line); a .bat is happiest with CRLF. Pin both so the
# committer's OS and each cloner's autocrlf setting cannot corrupt them.
*.command text eol=lf
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.bat     text eol=crlf
